  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A simple pendulum is displaced by a small angle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> and when it is released at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span>, it oscillates with simple harmonic motion (SHM) near the surface of planet X. The length of the pendulum is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"78\"></span> cm. The pendulum bob completes <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"17\"></span> full oscillations in a minute. </p>\n<p>a. Show that the time period of the oscillations is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.53\"></span> s.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>b. Calculate the gravitational field strength near the surface of planet X. Include an appropriate unit with your answer.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p>c. On the graph, sketch how the displacement of the pendulum bob varies with time.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>The pendulum is moved to planet Y where the acceleration of free fall is four times that of the acceleration of free fall on planet X. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> the pendulum is displaced by angle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> and released. </p>\n<p>d. On the graph, sketch how the displacement of the pendulum bob varies with time on planet Y.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>  [2]</p>"
  },
